.TH AVR\-GROUP\-MEMBER 1 "" "avr" "Avrea CLI"
.SH NAME
avr-group-member \- List, add and remove a group's members.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B avr group member
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]...
.SH DESCRIPTION
List, add and remove a group's members.
.PP
A change names each MEMBER by user ID (usr-...), @me for yourself, or an email address the member verified. Display names are not accepted: members choose them, so one can match the wrong person. `avr auth status` shows your user ID.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
add
Add members to a group.
.TP
list
List a group's direct members.
.TP
remove
Remove members from a group.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR avr (1),
.BR avr-group (1),
